          <div class="browser"><div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><div class="body"><strong>NYPL Explorer</strong><div class="tiles"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="meta"><span>Harvard Coursework · CSCI E-12</span><span class="year">Coursework</span></div>
        <h3>Exploring the New York Public Library’s digital collections.</h3>
        <span class="method hand">Coded from scratch</span>
        <p class="result"><strong>Live data</strong> from the NYPL API</p>
        <p>A working site for searching and browsing the NYPL Digital Collections using real records from its public API. I designed and coded the experience by hand as my first complete from-scratch web build.</p>
        <ul><li>HTML / CSS / JS</li><li>Public API</li><li>Responsive web</li><li>Shipped coursework</li></ul>
